{
  "case_id": "2016-16-529",
  "document_hash": "a872efe8bb09d8c5726b20d90c985100d0151e93c194775e15c0ee384d51ad16",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2016-16-529",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "a872efe8bb09d8c5726b20d90c985100d0151e93c194775e15c0ee384d51ad16",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a872efe8bb09-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument this morning first in Case 16-529, Kokesh v. The Securities and Exchange Commission."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-16-529",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "a872efe8bb09d8c5726b20d90c985100d0151e93c194775e15c0ee384d51ad16",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a872efe8bb09-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Counselor, before the 1970s -- and you haven't shown me anything to the contrary -- forfeiture was an in rem proceeding where the property was attached; the money, the bank account, a piece of property, a home, whatever, but it was not a personal action against an individual. So how do we get from that traditional understanding which governed this statute to your meaning today?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Adam Unikowsky)",
      "case_id": "2016-16-529",
      "confidence": 0.91,
      "document_hash": "a872efe8bb09d8c5726b20d90c985100d0151e93c194775e15c0ee384d51ad16",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a872efe8bb09-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, Your Honor, first of all, I think the legal standard is that if it has components of both a penal and remedial remedy, it's considered penal."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2016-16-529",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a872efe8bb09d8c5726b20d90c985100d0151e93c194775e15c0ee384d51ad16",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a872efe8bb09-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So I'm very happy on the facts of this particular case to defend our position that this is a forfeiture and as well as a penalty, I would say."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-16-529",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a872efe8bb09d8c5726b20d90c985100d0151e93c194775e15c0ee384d51ad16",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a872efe8bb09-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: But that -- but that might suggest something along the lines of what Justice Ginsburg suggested, that if the government, in fact, puts this money into the hands of victims, then it is compensatory; whereas if the government keeps it, it's not. And that the rule should follow, depending on which is true."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-16-529",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a872efe8bb09d8c5726b20d90c985100d0151e93c194775e15c0ee384d51ad16",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a872efe8bb09-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: It gets more complicated than that, because the money goes to the court -- MR. UNIKOWSKY: Yes. JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: -- according to the government, and it's the court that decides how the money will be paid out, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2016-16-529",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a872efe8bb09d8c5726b20d90c985100d0151e93c194775e15c0ee384d51ad16",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a872efe8bb09-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So this -- it depends. There's -- there's one statute on Fair Funds, and in some cases, you have disgorgements that go into there, and there's a Sarbanes-Oxley statute that directs the SEC to distribute that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2016-16-529",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a872efe8bb09d8c5726b20d90c985100d0151e93c194775e15c0ee384d51ad16",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a872efe8bb09-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "positions, because the government really has taken the position in its brief that disgorgement is a penalty for some reasons and not others."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "SEC",
      "case_id": "2016-16-529",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a872efe8bb09d8c5726b20d90c985100d0151e93c194775e15c0ee384d51ad16",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a872efe8bb09-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "For almost 50 years, courts have been ordering disgorgement in SEC enforcement actions to remedy unjust enrichment and put a defendant in the position he would have been in if he hadn't violated the law. Courts sometimes send that money to the Treasury, but when feasible, at the direction of the court, it's distributed to the injured victims, either by the court itself, by a trustee, by a receiver."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. GOLDENBERG",
      "case_id": "2016-16-529",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a872efe8bb09d8c5726b20d90c985100d0151e93c194775e15c0ee384d51ad16",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a872efe8bb09-0002-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. GOLDENBERG: $35 million."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-16-529",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a872efe8bb09d8c5726b20d90c985100d0151e93c194775e15c0ee384d51ad16",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a872efe8bb09-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: So what is the difference from restitution?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. GOLDENBERG",
      "case_id": "2016-16-529",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a872efe8bb09d8c5726b20d90c985100d0151e93c194775e15c0ee384d51ad16",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a872efe8bb09-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our argument is that under 2462, as the terms \"penalty\" and \"forfeiture\" should be understood under this Court's decision in Meeker, they both refer to doing something punitive, that disgorgement is not a penalty or a forfeiture under this provision."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2016-16-529",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a872efe8bb09d8c5726b20d90c985100d0151e93c194775e15c0ee384d51ad16",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a872efe8bb09-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why does the form, whether this is civil versus criminal, make all the difference?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. GOLDENBERG",
      "case_id": "2016-16-529",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a872efe8bb09d8c5726b20d90c985100d0151e93c194775e15c0ee384d51ad16",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a872efe8bb09-0002-0003",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Even if the Court were to rule that Section 2462 covered disgorgement, the government could still bring actions more than five years after bad conduct, seeking injunctions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2016-16-529",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a872efe8bb09d8c5726b20d90c985100d0151e93c194775e15c0ee384d51ad16",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a872efe8bb09-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We don't apply the canon in criminal cases, so why should we apply it in a case where the penalty is identical to what might be a criminal penalty?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAGAN",
      "case_id": "2016-16-529",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a872efe8bb09d8c5726b20d90c985100d0151e93c194775e15c0ee384d51ad16",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a872efe8bb09-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Unikowsky's standard is that if something is not solely remedial, then it's a penalty. Do you agree with that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. GOLDENBERG",
      "case_id": "2016-16-529",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a872efe8bb09d8c5726b20d90c985100d0151e93c194775e15c0ee384d51ad16",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a872efe8bb09-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I disagree with the principle that just because something has some deterrent effect or deterrent purpose, that that makes it a punishment, and that's a proposition that this Court has rejected a number of times, in its decision in Hudson, in its decision in Smith v. Doe, which is an ex post facto case, and it has overruled a decision on that -- some of the decisions that Petitioner cites' relied on."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GINSBURG",
      "case_id": "2016-16-529",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a872efe8bb09d8c5726b20d90c985100d0151e93c194775e15c0ee384d51ad16",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a872efe8bb09-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Narrow -- narrow construction of what?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. UNIKOWSKY",
      "case_id": "2016-16-529",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a872efe8bb09d8c5726b20d90c985100d0151e93c194775e15c0ee384d51ad16",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a872efe8bb09-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We are relying on the text of the statute. We think this is a forfeiture and is a penalty under the dictionary definitions of those terms."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-16-529",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a872efe8bb09d8c5726b20d90c985100d0151e93c194775e15c0ee384d51ad16",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a872efe8bb09-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
